{"name":"Firefly","hex":"#314643","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Firefly","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A locality in the MidCoast council area, eastern New South Wales, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Firefly"}],"entries":[{"title":"Firefly","blocks":[{"text":"The Lampyridae are a family of elateroid beetles with more than 2,400 described species, many of which are light-emitting. They are soft-bodied beetles commonly called fireflies, lightning bugs, or glowworms for their conspicuous emission of light, mainly during twilight, to attract mates. The type species is Lampyris noctiluca, the common glow-worm of Europe. Light production in the Lampyridae is thought to have originated as a warning signal that the larvae were distasteful. This ability to create light was then co-opted as a mating signal and, in a further development, adult female fireflies of the genus Photuris mimic the flash pattern of the Photinus beetle to trap their males as prey."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Photuris_lucicrescens.jpg/330px-Photuris_lucicrescens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefly"},{"title":"Firefly (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Firefly is a 2002 American space Western drama television series, created by writer and director Joss Whedon, under his Mutant Enemy Productions label. Whedon served as an executive producer, along with Tim Minear. The series is set in the year 2517, after the arrival of humans in a new star system, and follows the adventures of the renegade crew of Serenity, a \"Firefly-class\" spaceship. The ensemble cast portrays the nine characters living aboard Serenity. Whedon pitched the show as \"nine people looking into the blackness of space and seeing nine different things.\""}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/af/Fireflyopeninglogo.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefly_(TV_series)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Lampyris_Noctiluca_%28firefly%29_mating.gif/500px-Lampyris_Noctiluca_%28firefly%29_mating.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Lampyris_Noctiluca_%28firefly%29_mating.gif/500px-Lampyris_Noctiluca_%28firefly%29_mating.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALampyris_Noctiluca_(firefly)_mating.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Luciola4_crop.png/500px-Luciola4_crop.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Luciola4_crop.png/500px-Luciola4_crop.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A larviform female with light-emitting organs on her abdomen. Unlike larvae, she has compound eyes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALuciola4_crop.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Firefly_composite.jpg/500px-Firefly_composite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Firefly_composite.jpg/500px-Firefly_composite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photuris female by flash photography (above); by her own light (below)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFirefly_composite.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Leuchtk%C3%A4fer_-_Firefly.JPG/500px-Leuchtk%C3%A4fer_-_Firefly.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wi